            "name": "acquisition_system_id",
            "mustBeNonEmpty": false,
            "documentation": "The rig this channel group is read on -- the device half of v1's `devicestring` or a syncrule's device name. Every writer fills it today (Jess Haley 2026-10-22 [audit mechanical fixes 2]): a migrated probemap's channel groups, the two documents of a migrated filefind syncrule (resolved by session and name in did2.convert.resolveClockAlignment), and the Haley import's junction between a system and its recordings. DECIDED REQUIRED (#73 item 56); still declared optional here. The decided minting pass resolves a device name by (session, name) and, when no `acquisition_system` has that name, MINTS one whose `name` is the device name, so the edge always resolves and the rig's name lives in one place. (Until item 54 an unresolved name rode on `base.name`.)",
