            "queryable": true,
            "ontology": null,
            "documentation": "The document has three uses (Jess Haley 2026-10-22 [audit mechanical fixes 2]): the channel groups of a migrated probemap (one entry per channel-TYPE GROUP, as v1's devicestring stores them, 'mydevice:ai27-28,45,88;di1-4'); the two ends of a migrated filefind syncrule, which carry only `acquisition_system_id`; and the Haley import's per-system junction that a recording interaction points at, which carries only `acquisition_system_id`. `type` is scalar PER ENTRY because a group is by definition one type; `numbers` is the list. NOT equal-length parallel arrays -- the flat form repeats the type N times and discards the grouping the source actually stores. Empty when the document only names its system.",
