                    "ontology": null,
                    "documentation": "The channel type, a term under NCIT:C44170 Channel (Jess Haley 2026-10-22 [channel types]): analog input channel (v1 `ai`), analog output channel (`ao`), digital input channel (`di`), digital output channel (`do`), time channel (`t`), auxiliary input channel (`ax`), event channel (`e`), marker channel (`mk`), Metadata (`md`), Text (`tx`). The migrator maps each v1 prefix to its term, and NDI's vintage map maps term to prefix for its readers; that map lives in their code, not in the term registry, and code matches a channel type by its node. The eight read modes NDI derives from a channel at read time (dep den dimp dimn aep aen aimp aimn) are not channel types and get no terms. Bound, required (#73 audit 2 D5).",
